==English==

===Etymology===
Shortened from {{term|acquis communautaire|lang=en}}, from {{etyl|fr|en}} {{term|acquis||that which has been acquired or obtained|lang=fr}} + {{term|communautaire||of the community|lang=fr}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/aˈkiː/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US}} {{IPA|/ɑˈki/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-}}

# The accumulated [[legislation]], legal [[act]]s, and court [[decision]]s which constitute the [[total]] [[body]] of [[EU]] [[law]].
# The accumulated legislation and decisions of any international community.
#* '''2013''', Gerhard Erasmus, ''Redirecting the Tripartite Free Trade Agreement negotiations?'', Trade Law Centre, page 6:
#*:  In the context of the Tripartite Free Trade Agreement ['''acquis'''] means that the negotiations should start from the point at which... the COMESA, EAC and SADC trade negotiations have reached.

